WEBVTT

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:12.784
The Fair Labor Standards Act, a federal wage and hour law, requires Cisco to track all hours worked for non-exempt employees, including interns and part-time employees.

00:00:12.784 --> 00:00:16.831
Tracking time ensures compliance, and accurate overtime pay.

00:00:18.181 --> 00:00:27.845
Your status can change during your time at Cisco, for example when your job role changes, or when you move to a state whose laws are stricter than federal law.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:32.872
To check your own status, look at your offer letter.

00:00:32.872 --> 00:00:40.012
Or open Workday, go to your profile, choose Job, and on the Position tab, read FLSA Exemption Status.

00:00:40.012 --> 00:00:43.688
No, eligible for overtime, means you are non-exempt.

00:00:43.688 --> 00:00:47.435
Yes, not eligible for overtime, means you are exempt.

00:00:48.785 --> 00:00:54.140
This course is for non-exempt employees who track their time, and for the leaders who manage them.
